<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African April M3 money supply grows 15.44 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African April M3 money supply grows 15.44 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 15.44 percent in April, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>March M3 growth was revised to 16.46 percent from a preliminary 16.39 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 16.95 percent, preliminary figures showed, against 15.95 percent in March.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast M3 year-on-year growth of 16.70 percent while private credit was seen expanding 16.40 percent.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>April 1997 preliminary M3 growth -- 15.44 percent</p>
<p>April 1997 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 16.95 percent</p>
<p>					   Mar'97	   Feb'97</p>
<p>M3  revised			    16.46	    15.88</p>
<p>M2    &quot;				  17.84	    17.51</p>
<p>M1    &quot;				  30.07	    29.21</p>
<p>Private sector credit growth     15.95	    17.34</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (rand billions)</p>
<p>			     Apr'97 (prel)  Mar'97(rev)  Feb'97 (rev)</p>
<p>M3 unadjusted	    336.39	   336.78	 327.60</p>
<p>M3 seasonally adj.     335.78	   333.65	 327.39</p>
<p>Private sector credit  386.98	   383.13	 379.49</p>
<p>M3 annualised growth rate from base of guideline</p>
<p>				16.67	   18.72	  16.83</p>
<p>(1996 guideline range 6-10 pct)</p>
